{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2019-11-08 11:30:00', 'title': 'Abbvie Submits Supplemental NDA To U.S. FDA For Imbruvica In Combination With Rituximab', 'text': 'ABBVIE SUBMITS SUPPLEMENTAL NEW DRUG APPLICATION TO U.S. FDA FOR IMBRUVICA (IBRUTINIB) IN COMBINATION WITH RITUXIMAB FOR THE TREATMENT OF PREVIOUSLY UNTREATED, YOUNGER ADULTS WITH CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA.ABBVIE INC - SUBMISSION IS BASED ON POSITIVE RESULTS FROM PHASE 3 E1912 CLINICAL TRIAL.'}
{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2019-11-08 22:30:00', 'title': 'AbbVie Inc. Submits Supplemental New Drug Application to U.S. FDA for IMBRUVICA (Ibrutinib)', 'text': 'AbbVie Inc. announced it has submitted a supplemental New Drug Application (sNDA) to the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for IMBRUVICA (ibrutinib) in combination with rituximab for the first-line treatment of younger patients (70 years old or younger) with chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) or small lymphocytic lymphoma (SLL). The submission is based on results from the Phase 3 E1912 study – designed and conducted by the ECOG-ACRIN Cancer Research Group (ECOG-ACRIN) and sponsored by the National Cancer Institute (NCI), part of the National Institutes of Health. The study showed significantly improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS) in patients treated with IMBRUVICA plus rituximab, compared to those treated with fludarabine, cyclophosphamide and rituximab (FCR). Safety data were consistent with the known safety profile of IMBRUVICA. The application is being reviewed under the Real-Time Oncology Review (RTOR) pilot program, which allows the FDA to review data before the applicant formally submits the complete application. The program is designed to explore a more efficient review process to ensure safe and effective treatments become available to patients earlier, while maintaining quality of review.'}
