{'symbol': 'HPQ', 'date': '2019-11-08 22:30:00', 'title': 'HP Provides Information to its Shareholders', 'text': 'On November 8, 2019, HP Inc. announced that it is still reviewing the takeover offer of Xerox Holdings Corporation in order to determine if it is in the best interest of the Company. The Company added that its board reportedly is not sure yet whether a sale is the best option at the moment. The Company also stated that it is not in a hurry to issue an opinion on the takeover approach, Xerox Holdings would prefer to receive an answer within a week.'}
{'symbol': 'ILMN', 'date': '2019-11-08 22:30:00', 'title': 'Lexent Bio Enters Partnership with Illumina to Develop an in Vitro Diagnostic Kit', 'text': "Lexent Bio, Inc. announced a non-exclusive partnership with Illumina, Inc. to develop an in-vitro diagnostic kit for Lexent's future portfolio of next-generation sequencing (NGS)-based cancer diagnostics. The IVD kit under development will expand the availability of Lexent's assay, currently in development as Confera™ Dx, for monitoring therapeutic response for patients with certain solid tumor cancers and for monitoring minimal residual disease. The Confera Dx assay will be launched in the US market as a laboratory developed test (LDT) performed by Lexent in a CLIA-certified laboratory, with the distributable IVD kit to follow. Lexent believes the Confera Dx response monitoring system will be well suited for distribution as an IVD kit with FDA Clearance, making it available for hospitals and health systems to run in their local laboratories across the United States, and eventually around the world. Under this agreement, Lexent will develop the IVD kit to run on Illumina's NextSeq™ 550Dx System. Lexent will be responsible for obtaining the necessary regulatory approvals for the IVD kit and for subsequent commercialization. Illumina will sell the NextSeq 550Dx System and associated sequencing consumables with customer service and support as needed."}
